# =============================================================================
# Xvfb Virtual Framebuffer Configuration
# =============================================================================
# This template generates the configuration file for Xvfb (X Virtual Framebuffer).
# Xvfb is an X server that runs on a machine that may not have a display,
# input devices, etc., but can still satisfy the needs of X clients.
#
# The configuration is typically consumed by a systemd service unit or
# an init script that reads these variables and constructs the command line.
# =============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISPLAY_NUM
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The X server display number to listen on.
# Xvfb will listen on :N. Must be a non-negative integer.
# Example: 99 results in listening on :99
#
# Variable: server_num
# Schema Default: 99
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISPLAY_NUM={{ server_num | default(99) }}

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXTRA_ARGS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional command-line arguments passed to Xvfb.
# Supports various Xvfb options such as -screen, -pixdepths, -fbdir, -shmem,
# -linebias, -blackpixel, -whitepixel, etc.
#
# Common usage: "-screen 0 1280x1024x24 -shmem"
#
# Variable: extra_args
# Schema Default: '-screen 0 1280x1024x24 -shmem'
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXTRA_ARGS="{{ extra_args | default('-screen 0 1280x1024x24 -shmem') }}"